    stem: "This edited extract deals with the career of Samuel Louis Crommelin. Read it and answer the questions which follow.\n\nSamuel Louis Crommelin was born in Picardy, France, in 1652. In the late 1690s we find him running a linen production centre, with a bleach-yard along Bridge Street, in Lisburn, Co. Down.\nOn 20 April, 1707, a fire gutted most of the town centre compelling him to consider moving. However, in 1715, he had the good fortune to receive a government pension of 400 pounds. Expanding his business, he set up sailcloth production in Waterford, Cork and elsewhere.\nCrommelin died on 17 July, 1727, having – along with other Huguenot businessmen – contributed significantly to the growth of the Irish linen industry.",
