    section: "2", questionRef: "2022 OL Early Modern Section 2 Topic 4 A Q5",
    stem: "This edited extract relates to the poet Dáibhí Ó Bruadair. Read it and answer the questions which follow.\n\nThe poet Dáibhí Ó Bruadair was one of the last practitioners of the poems of the bardic schools. At least eighty of his poems have been preserved in Irish manuscripts.\nHis work included political poems and satires in which he scorns the lowbred Cromwellians. In eulogies he praises his patrons: the MacCarthys and Barrys in Co. Cork, and the Fitzgeralds and Bourkes in Co. Limerick. In elegies he mourns their deaths.",
